    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey` and made the endpoint return it.\n\n**New identity model**\n- `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId` \u2014 implemented in a new `IdentityKeys` helper (`forRequest` for the incoming DTO, `forOwner` for stored owners), so a create is rejected with **409 only when a new owner's whole key equals an existing owner's**.\n- Because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now produce different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match conflicts. This is the intended behaviour change.\n- Extracted the `householdId` derivation into a shared `Households` helper so the value folded into the key is byte-for-byte the same one `AssignHousehold` assigns.\n\n**Wiring**\n- New `RequireUniqueIdentity` function (single duplicate check) replaces the `unique` \u2192 `uniqueEmail` \u2192 `household` steps in `owners.POST.yml` with one `identity` step.\n- New checked `DuplicateIdentityException` + handler + escalation YAML (409 Conflict), mirroring the existing pattern.\n- Deleted the now-obsolete `RequireUniqueTelephone/Email/Household` functions and the three `Duplicate{Telephone,Email,Household}` exceptions/handlers/escalation YAMLs.\n\n**Returning `identityKey`**\n- Added a read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (drives the generated DTO).\n- Added an `OwnerMapper` mapping that computes it via `IdentityKeys.forOwner(owner)`, so it's returned on both create and read.\n\nThe one behavioural nuance worth flagging: the test's collision case (same telephone, no email, no shared household \u2192 both keys `+61\u2026||`) correctly rejects, and the household component uses each owner's *actual* `householdId` field (empty unless `sharesHousehold` was set), not a name+address hash of every owner \u2014 which is what makes same-household/different-phone pairs pass.",
